<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump visits Ireland, says unification would be 'fantastic'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:458096e6f77cc133777af1c02254b06b891f75e531d48ee966dffda0de2ddc31</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-visits-ireland-says-unification-would-be-fantastic/a-79244685--23dd10281a51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-visits-ireland-says-unification-would-be-fantastic/a-79244685?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's trip to Ireland to watch a golf tournament has also included meetings with leaders there.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Corals as climate archive: Are El Ninos intensifying?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4334f8324c63b22a3fc6b02191d339118f9804861ba36ea39363c25fcc8226e</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T08:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-ninos-intensifying/a-79243425--052f407fd862.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-ninos-intensifying/a-79243425?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Records from the past few decades show that, during this period, El Nino events have been frequent and often extreme. But is this normal, or is it the result of climate change? Corals can give us a clear indication.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uber leaves two key African markets — and their drivers in despair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d75febe91341d0aef8ef2052d669a057e044f7b1b08a0330f8e9061f9f6c253e</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T07:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-two-key-african-markets-and-their-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189--bdbc88dc3498.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-two-key-african-markets-and-their-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Uber's departure from Nigeria and Uganda has left countless customers high and dry. But what about drivers? With fuel prices, maintenance, and other operating costs rising, many say they're struggling to make a living.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's drone war comes to Moldova and Romania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0bf53e38d45f37393eb826a007d8ac42204a95593b33e73a7105cfba7c7940bd</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T06:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591--15076a5f335b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Incursions by Russian drones into Moldovan and Romanian airspace are increasingly common. This week the Ukrainian president's plane was stopped from taking off from Chisinau. Observers suspect the attacks are deliberate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>DW exclusive: Zelenskyy offers to meet Putin at G20 in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:476d351186d6a04a054d05c2ca7dbe8425ed47ad8622aa937d4dfdd75a12efc6</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-exclusive-zelenskyy-offers-to-meet-putin-at-g20-in-miami/a-79241703--3aacfd955f7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-exclusive-zelenskyy-offers-to-meet-putin-at-g20-in-miami/a-79241703?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In an interview with DW, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said his country was in a strong position to negotiate and offered to meet Vladimir Putin in Miami.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran pursues cautious escalation ahead of US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56552e0fac3024dad2715130c103ae01af136ae53cf019b09629d92be481a6fa</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-pursues-cautious-escalation-ahead-of-us-midterms/a-79237061--fcf56cfd7af3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-pursues-cautious-escalation-ahead-of-us-midterms/a-79237061?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tehran appears to be boosting pressure on Washington ahead of the crucial midterm vote, but shows little desire to return to a full-scale war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's BRICS strategy tested with Xi, Putin set to visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97efd9faae3b65a47e03f01926dcd9291921fde2bf18c6d347fb178f05c2c07c</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-brics-strategy-tested-with-xi-putin-set-to-visit/a-79231879--3d59ee566cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-brics-strategy-tested-with-xi-putin-set-to-visit/a-79231879?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New Delhi's "America Plus" approach sees India deepening its ties with China and Russia, while also trying to keep BRICS from turning into an anti-Western platform.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war: Saudi-Houthi escalation intensifies Yemen conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccf3915372e320ce7264f51657476a3e4e55c0cfa8bf471659f0f655bbd808f6</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-saudi-houthi-escalation-intensifies-yemen-conflict/a-79226627--c5b66c310724.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-saudi-houthi-escalation-intensifies-yemen-conflict/a-79226627?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Houthi takeovers of Mokha, Dhubab and Perim in the Bab el-Mandeb Strait threaten to push Yemen deeper into the Middle East war. The Iran-backed group has made advances against Yemen's government and Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's Kim Jong Un doesn't need a US deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daeb60e067d52da3910e84d8cb71f88bb059e503d80d21cb8c7cde6b965ae6cc</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854--e7f102464964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's overtures to North Korea's dictator have gone nowhere, with an emboldened Pyongyang accelerating its nuclear program and solidifying alliances with Russia and China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Turks in Germany anxious after AfD wins in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e903fef67c19d3806aebb4ce4034d65a75f577ed766b70437d7f5512541cd178</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764--9bdd69d84853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party's win in Saxony-Anhalt has alarmed people of Turkish origin in eastern states. Will workers and business owners abandon the increasingly AfD-friendly region for the more welcoming west?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong Tiananmen activists jailed for up to 7 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8edb2a41aeefd93620a1cbe9bef11cd856b92e88931b5fcc8b6c54ad305b1e9d</id><updated>2026-09-13T04:59:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-tiananmen-activists-jailed-for-up-to-7-years/a-79224243--b40cd2f6f0ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-tiananmen-activists-jailed-for-up-to-7-years/a-79224243?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three pro-democracy activists who organized annual commemorations of China's deadly 1989 Tiananmen crackdown were charged under Hong Kong's Beijing-backed national security law.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
